{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"## PR #11: your read is right — it's the honest-history PR, not the clean-slate one\n\nIt deliberately leaves the seams showing, and your approve-then-cleanup plan is exactly what I'd do. Here's the actual cruft inventory so the cleanup PR has a checklist, sorted by what it's waiting on:\n\n**Deletable immediately after merge (pure debt):**\n- The pure pipe-through files — `canonical.ts`, `git.ts`, `reanchor.ts`, `reanchor-suggest.ts`, `forge/forge.ts`, `redact/apply.ts` are nothing but `export { … } from \"annals\"`. Internal code should import `\"annals\"` directly; the handful of symbols turnbridge needs (`findRepo`, `git`, `gitUserIdentity`, `reAnchorDraft`, …) can be re-exported straight from `index.ts`.\n- The README's \"As of 0.26.0 the storage machinery moved…\" paragraph reads as a changelog entry; fold it into a proper architecture sentence.\n- The retired `design/extension-governance` branch.\n\n**Deletable only after you run the wipe (order matters here):**\n- `scripts/wipe-ev1-history.sh` itself.\n- The ev1 tolerance in `schema.ts`'s `fromAnnals` (the `legacy` lifting of top-level `actor`/producer fields) — that exists solely to read pre-extraction lines, and removing it before the wipe would break `cledger log` on your current mixed refs.\n\n**Not cruft — keep (worth saying so the cleanup PR doesn't overreach):**\n- `ledger.ts` (the namespace pin) and the namespace-binding wrappers in `store.ts`/`transport.ts`/`review.ts`/`redact/config|scan|known-secrets.ts` — anything that takes a plain `RepoInfo` and attaches the namespace, plus the `toAnnals`/`fromAnnals` translation. That *is* cledger now: the vocabulary and its binding. They could be consolidated into fewer files for taste, but they can't become direct imports.\n- `ConversationRef` alias — until turnbridge's branch lands and it migrates to `StreamRef`, then deletable.\n- `file:../annals` — swap to a version range in the cleanup PR only if annals is on npm by then.\n\nSo the sequence: **merge PR #11 → run the wipe script → cleanup PR.** One operational note for the merge: use a regular merge commit, not squash. This session's own captured conversation is anchored to the `annals-extraction` commits; a squash rewrites those commits away and makes the ledger lean on the auto-re-anchor machinery, while a merge commit keeps every anchor reachable from `main` with zero drama. (Your recent PRs are merge commits anyway.)\n\n## Prompt for the turnbridge agent\n\n```\nContext: cledger has been re-architected (conversation-ledger PR #11, branch\n`annals-extraction`). Its storage layer is now a separate public package,\n`annals` (github.com/evintunador/annals; local checkout at ../annals). What\nchanged for turnbridge: the ledger envelope field `conversation` is renamed\n`stream`, event ids are `ev2-…`, the schema line is `annals/v1`. cledger's\nflat surface (actor, producer.source/model/provider, appendEvents/readEvents\nfrom \"conversation-ledger\") is otherwise UNCHANGED — a translation layer in\ncledger folds those into the new envelope, so you code against the same API\nas before. The `cledger` CLI on this machine is globally npm-linked to the\nrepo checkout, so it already runs the new code.\n\nStep 0 — land the compat branch. This repo has a local, unpushed branch\n`annals-cledger`: one mechanical commit (conversation→stream at the envelope\ntouchpoints, 91/91 tests green). Nothing here compiles against cledger\nwithout it. Rebase on main if needed, push it, open a PR, and treat it as\nthe base for everything below.\n\nStep 1 — delete the fetch-everything workaround. src/conversations.ts:36-40\nfetches all events and narrows in inScope() because readEvents' kind filter\nused to be exact-match. readEvents now accepts\n`kind: [\"conversation_turn\", \"reasoning\"]` (and also new `tool` and\n`linkRel` filters). Replace the workaround; keep the tests honest.\n\nStep 2 — docs/TODO_HANDOFF.md section A is superseded; update it. The\ncledger extension-governance handoff shipped in different form: the\nregistration/discovery mechanism was deliberately NOT built. The contract\nis: a third-party kind is identified by (producer.tool, kind); whoever emits\na vocabulary publishes its reader — for `continuation` that reader is\nturnbridge's own readLineage/ContinuationRecord export, which context-graph\nwill import rather than parsing content by hand. Rewrite section A as a\nshort pointer to annals' README and this contract.\n\nStep 3 — work section B of docs/TODO_HANDOFF.md, which stays entirely in\nthis repo. Suggested order, cheap to deep:\n  a. Read producer.model / producer.provider instead of actor.id for model\n     identity (LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md §1). opencode.ts:217-221 currently\n     guesses provider by string-splitting the model id; producer.provider is\n     the stated answer, and unset means \"source didn't say\", never infer.\n  b. Marker reduction (POLICY_SPLIT.md §4): opencode's reasoning parts are\n     plaintext, so stop injecting `[visible thinking]` on the opencode path —\n     emit a native reasoning part. Claude/Codex paths cannot change.\n  c. Move human-facing disclosures (model substitution, ancestor\n     unavailable, size) out of the fabricated transcript into plan.notes;\n     only the import notice belongs in model context.\n  d. Probe whether Claude's system/attachment lines reach model context\n     (docs/specs/claude-session-format.md:74,:196 disagree with cledger's\n     context_injection framing); if they do, the import notice can stop\n     being a counterfeit user turn.\n  e. The big one — multi-hop re-sourcing (LINEAGE §2-3a): when bridging a\n     conversation whose prefix is itself an import, walk parentOf\n     transitively and render each turn from the conversation where it\n     ORIGINATED, never from a copy (\"copy from the original, never from the\n     previous copy\"). Prerequisite: record the ordered source event ids in\n     the continuation event's content at fabricate time (content is\n     turnbridge-owned; no cledger change needed). Decisions already leaning\n     but to be confirmed as you go: render \"as it would have been\" (undo\n     turnbridge's own transport damage, don't invent history); degrade\n     gracefully to the copy when the ancestor is unreachable, with\n     disclosure; collapse ancestral import notices into one that names the\n     whole chain.\n\nHouse rules: this repo is PUBLIC and this conversation is captured by\ncledger into git notes that also get pushed. Never type a whole\nformat-valid credential (real or fake) into code, docs, commit messages, or\nchat — keyword-shaped fakes need an uppercase FAKE/EXAMPLE/TESTONLY marker\ninside the value, and format-valid test tokens must be stored split so that\nNO individual fragment is matchable by a public secret scanner on its own\n(a Slack-shaped fragment in a fixture just fired a GitGuardian alert for\nexactly this). If the pre-push scan reports findings, stop and hand the\nqueue to the human; do not read flagged content into the session.\n```\n\nTwo notes on it: step 0 has the agent push the branch itself (it's still local-only here), and I left PR-#11-merge out of its preconditions — the branch builds against cledger's `annals-extraction` via the `file:` link regardless of whether you've merged yet.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"annals-extraction","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"d822870bf6a1f6bc481e56557deffd2045a36202","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-a84084def75d89005483ba3a0c4e8ae59e5dda832f78e2d6104a5e171cf229a2","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-fable-5","session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.267"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-10T03:16:46.842Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"apiBlockI