{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"All four answered, with the changes shipped:\n\n**1. Meta and secrets — you're right, and I flipped it.** The pre-extraction envelope never redaction-walked `actor` or the producer fields, so walking `meta` was a new behavior I'd introduced, not a preserved safety property. Worse, meta is where UUIDs, session ids, and digests live — exactly what entropy/keyword rules false-positive on, and compounding false findings is this project's characteristic bug. `meta` is now **not** walked by redaction or the scan, with the contract documented in the schema and README: structured provenance only (ids, names, labels), never free text — anything that could carry source material or a secret belongs in `content`/`raw`, where the redaction stack applies. Same contract `resolved` already had.\n\n**2. cledger updated accordingly?** Yes — that was last round's translation layer, and it carried through this change untouched: cledger's flat `actor`/`producer.model` surface folds into `meta` on write and lifts back on read, adapters and CLI byte-identical, and your live install (the npm link) is already running it. Both suites re-ran green after the meta change (annals 150, cledger 90).\n\n**3. Pushed to public — yes, both.**\n- **annals**: created `github.com/evintunador/annals` (public) and pushed `main`.\n- **cledger**: pushed `annals-extraction` and opened **PR #11** → https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/11. The pre-push scan gate ran and passed — the notes ref went to origin clean, nothing held for review.\n- Not pushed: turnbridge's `annals-cledger` branch (you asked about the two; say the word and I'll push + PR that too). Also remember npm publishing is still blocked until annals is on npm and cledger's `file:../annals` becomes a version range.\n\n**4. The original turnbridge ask — accomplished, and mostly superseded.** The handoff's concrete items all landed: `readEvents` now takes `tool`, `kind` as an array (the exact papercut behind turnbridge's fetch-everything workaround at `conversations.ts:36`), and `linkRel` (the filter context-graph's edge extraction wanted); the `ensureTransport` side effect is documented with its existing opt-out; and the `(producer.tool, kind)` contract is now annals' documented extension model. The registration/discovery item (Decision 4) was deliberately dissolved rather than built — the split made \"store validates the envelope, each producer owns and publishes its vocabulary's reader\" the answer, which is the outcome that doc was groping toward. Two optional follow-ups remain, both turnbridge-side and neither blocking: swap its `inScope()` workaround for the new kind-array filter, and the section-B items from its own TODO (reading `producer.model`/`provider` instead of `actor.id`, and the copy-from-the-original multi-hop fix), which you scoped out of these sessions.\n\nresult: meta is now unwalked with a documented provenance-only contract (your instinct was right — matches pre-extraction behavior and avoids entropy false-positives); annals is public at github.com/evintunador/annals, cledger's extraction is pushed as PR #11 with a clean scan gate; the original turnbridge handoff items (tool/kind[]/linkRel filters, transport disclosure, pair-key contract) are all delivered, with the registry item deliberately dissolved by the split.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"annals-extraction","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"d822870bf6a1f6bc481e56557deffd2045a36202","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-273866b1cbf418c73052684e03f38d6c84a3ab4207b9ac0373ccff949481438b","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-fable-5","session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.263"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-08T00:16:29.142Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw"